{"assets":["/statement-assets/90946ceaa54fb64e162087cbdb5305bc3171615514b026b28856a5785d6bd48c.png","/statement-assets/1427d0547519ce2d143f15c5e6fa01f472eaaf12c0e0f174b8d531231f6eeb9d.png","/statement-assets/646dbb1b7f7c5628aebcbddefa203fa87b24e9747f545ca1cf4055370d5f0c9f.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1823","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"F. Random Walk"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given a tree consisting of $$$n$$$ vertices and $$$n - 1$$$ edges, and each vertex $$$v$$$ has a counter $$$c(v)$$$ assigned to it."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Initially, there is a chip placed at vertex $$$s$$$ and all counters, except $$$c(s)$$$, are set to $$$0$$$; $$$c(s)$$$ is set to $$$1$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Your goal is to place the chip at vertex $$$t$$$. You can achieve it by a series of moves. Suppose right now the chip is placed at the vertex $$$v$$$. In one move, you do the following:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":true},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" choose one of neighbors $$$to$$$ of vertex $$$v$$$ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"uniformly at random"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" ($$$to$$$ is neighbor of $$$v$$$ if and only if there is an edge $$$\\{v, to\\}$$$ in the tree); "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" move the chip to vertex $$$to$$$ and increase $$$c(to)$$$ by $$$1$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You'll repeat the move above until you reach the vertex $$$t$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each vertex $$$v$$$ calculate the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"expected value"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of $$$c(v)$$$ modulo $$$998\\,244\\,353$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains three integers $$$n$$$, $$$s$$$ and $$$t$$$ ($$$2 \\le n \\le 2 \\cdot 10^5$$$; $$$1 \\le s, t \\le n$$$; $$$s \\neq t$$$) — number of vertices in the tree and the starting and finishing vertices."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Next $$$n - 1$$$ lines contain edges of the tree: one edge per line. The $$$i$$$-th line contains two integers $$$u_i$$$ and $$$v_i$$$ ($$$1 \\le u_i, v_i \\le n$$$; $$$u_i \\neq v_i$$$), denoting the edge between the nodes $$$u_i$$$ and $$$v_i$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It's guaranteed that the given edges form a tree."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print $$$n$$$ numbers: "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"expected values"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of $$$c(v)$$$ modulo $$$998\\,244\\,353$$$ for each $$$v$$$ from $$$1$$$ to $$$n$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Formally, let $$$M = 998\\,244\\,353$$$. It can be shown that the answer can be expressed as an irreducible fraction $$$\\frac{p}{q}$$$, where $$$p$$$ and $$$q$$$ are integers and $$$q \\not \\equiv 0 \\pmod{M}$$$. Output the integer equal to $$$p \\cdot q^{-1} \\bmod M$$$. In other words, output such an integer $$$x$$$ that $$$0 \\le x \\lt M$$$ and $$$x \\cdot q \\equiv p \\pmod{M}$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3 1 3\n1 2\n2 3\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n2 2 1 \n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4 1 3\n1 2\n2 3\n1 4\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4 2 1 2 \n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n8 2 6\n6 4\n6 2\n5 4\n3 1\n2 3\n7 4\n8 2\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n1 3 2 0 0 1 0 1 \n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The tree from the first example is shown below: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/90946ceaa54fb64e162087cbdb5305bc3171615514b026b28856a5785d6bd48c.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" Let's calculate expected value $$$E[c(1)]$$$: "},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$P(c(1) = 0) = 0$$$, since $$$c(1)$$$ is set to $$$1$$$ from the start. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$P(c(1) = 1) = \\frac{1}{2}$$$, since there is the only one series of moves that leads $$$c(1) = 1$$$. It's $$$1 \\rightarrow 2 \\rightarrow 3$$$ with probability $$$1 \\cdot \\frac{1}{2}$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$P(c(1) = 2) = \\frac{1}{4}$$$: the only path is $$$1 \\rightarrow_{1} 2 \\rightarrow_{0.5} 1 \\rightarrow_{1} 2 \\rightarrow_{0.5} 3$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$P(c(1) = 3) = \\frac{1}{8}$$$: the only path is $$$1 \\rightarrow_{1} 2 \\rightarrow_{0.5} 1 \\rightarrow_{1} 2 \\rightarrow_{0.5} 1 \\rightarrow_{1} 2 \\rightarrow_{0.5} 3$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$P(c(1) = i) = \\frac{1}{2^i}$$$ in general case. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"kind":"text","text":" As a result, $$$E[c(1)] = \\sum\\limits_{i=1}^{\\infty}{i \\frac{1}{2^i}} = 2$$$."},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Image of tree in second test"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/1427d0547519ce2d143f15c5e6fa01f472eaaf12c0e0f174b8d531231f6eeb9d.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Image of tree in third test"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/646dbb1b7f7c5628aebcbddefa203fa87b24e9747f545ca1cf4055370d5f0c9f.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"F","problemCode":"1823F","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1823/problem/F"}